-- title:
--   Finiteness of the Γ(q)∩Γ₀(M') level-automorphism group
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity $\xi$, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota_0 : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota_0(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of $q$-expansions over $\mathbb{Q}$ for the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ attached to $H = \ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times\big)$; that is, $K$ is the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of that field under $\mathbb{Q}\to L$. Let $G \le K \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[L]} K$ be the subgroup generated by those $L$-automorphisms $\tau$ of $K$ for which some $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ lies in $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and satisfies [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), i.e.: for every weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$, all modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ for the subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}(2,\mathbb{R})$ attached to $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M', H)$, all integral power series $p_f, p_g$ whose images under $\mathbb{Z}\to\mathbb{C}$ are the $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$ at width $1$, with $p_g$ nonzero as a Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$, every $x \in K$ whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ is the coefficientwise image of $p_f/p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, one has $\iota_*(\tau x)\cdot (g\mid_k \delta)^{\wedge} = (f\mid_k \delta)^{\wedge}$ as Laurent series over $\mathbb{C}$, where $\widehat{\ }$ denotes the $q$-expansion at width $1$ and $\delta =$ `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹` is the matrix $\begin{pmatrix} a & b/(q\ell) \\ (q\ell)c & d\end{pmatrix}$ built from the entries $a,b,c,d$ of $\gamma^{-1}$. The conclusion is that $G$ is finite and that $\#G$ divides $\ell(\ell^2-1)$.
--
--   The bound $\ell(\ell^2-1)$ is the order of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)$, and the result expresses that the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ generate a group that factors through the reduction of that congruence subgroup modulo $\ell$. It is used in the further analysis of the rigid-level function field $K$, in particular in the statements about level-stable charts and about inertia and invariants attached to $K$.
